# nr-office-engine-qa-finalize-dispatch: qa, finalize, save and close, the tool call's dispatch and the engine entry point (modules mixdog-office::actions, ::dispatch and ::engine)

Written without cargo: nothing below has been compiled (rustfmt parsed every file; the twin test replays a recording made by running the recorder
against C:/Project/mixdog, which ran). The modules are the library the Office tool's worker method (nr-office-worker-office-run) and the skill
scripts (source-extract, qc-pages) call; this task registers no protocol method and no service, so nothing is removed from SERVICE_PENDING in
compose_flip.rs.

It calls what the earlier fragments of the track add, so they are applied first: nr-office-engine-open-create.wire (`pub mod create; mode; open;
working_copy;` in session/mod.rs), nr-office-engine-snapshot.wire, nr-office-engine-inspect.wire, nr-office-engine-render.wire,
nr-office-engine-transactions-batch.wire (`pub mod batch; pub mod transactions;`) and nr-office-engine-author-actions.wire (`pub mod author;`, and the
Cargo lines it lists: mixdog-core-api, mixdog-fonts, mixdog-office-author, mixdog-pdf, mixdog-raster).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs
After the modules the earlier fragments add, and extending the crate documentation by one line ("[`actions`] is `qa`, `finalize`, `save` and `close`;
[`dispatch`] answers one call of the tool; [`engine`] is the entry point a process calls."):

    pub mod actions;
    pub mod dispatch;
    pub mod engine;

